# The checks the "standard" ruleset on master requires.
#
# scripts/check-required-contexts.sh (the lint job and `make check`) fails
# when these lines and the pull-request jobs of the `workflow` files
# disagree, in either direction. Add a job to one of these workflows and
# its name goes here in the same pull request, and in the ruleset:
#
#   gh api repos/neb-abera/aberaTech/rulesets/3113290 \
#     --jq '.rules[] | select(.type=="required_status_checks")'
#
# workflow <path>   a workflow whose pull-request jobs gate merges
# check <name>      a job name, as the job reports it
workflow .github/workflows/client-checks.yml
workflow .github/workflows/codeql.yml
workflow .github/workflows/security-scan.yml
check Compose database boots healthy
check End-to-end, in the container
check Lint and format, in the container
check Production image, in the container
check Scheduling unit tests, in the container
check Type check and unit tests, in the container
check analyze (actions)
check analyze (csharp)
check analyze (javascript-typescript)
check container scan (trivy)
check dast (ZAP baseline)
check dependency review
check lint (actionlint + shellcheck)
